    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on a few high-upside leverage points, led by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who commands the highest score of the day at 78.31. Despite facing a lefty, his elite contact profile and favorable #2 spot in the order make him an anchor. Close behind is **Bryson Stott** (72.63), who benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against a struggling pitcher in a park that enhances his specific platoon profile, and **Taylor Ward** (71.19), whose leadoff assignment against a vulnerable lefty makes him a premium play. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) also projects as a strong start, with park factors boosting his underlying xwOBA to make him a reliable source of power today.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision was bypassing **Geraldo Perdomo**. While his score of 43.08 keeps him in the marginal category, he was ultimately left out because he lacks the explosive SB ceiling required to move him ahead of the active middle-infield starters like **Masyn Winn** and **Bryson Stott**. We are also keeping a close eye on the risk profile of **Tyler Freeman** (46.71); while he earns a spot due to his prime batting position, he faces the toughest test of the day against a truly elite arm, which suppresses his projection. The bottom of the lineup features **Drew Gilbert** (41.52) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (50.00), who are on a short leash given the scarcity of our daily game caps and the need to preserve roster flexibility.\n\nWe continue to manage our bench depth with **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** both sidelined on the IL, limiting our options for late-game defensive substitutions or pinch-hit scenarios. The strategy remains clear: prioritize the high-efficiency slots against weaker SP_xERA arms and maintain our focus on the stolen base category, where players like **Daulton Varsho**\u2014who receives a bump here due to the opponent's slow delivery\u2014provide critical value that doesn't always show up in standard volume stats. Keep an eye on any late weather shifts, as these could easily swing the marginal scores of our bottom-third starters into sub-40 territory, triggering immediate benching to preserve our season-long caps.",
